  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9f2e8e5b57bd4bd99f33dd56077c2d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: KB_012_ReceiptLookupFails
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: POSTechSupport::POSTechSupport.Data.KnowledgeArticleSO
  articleId: KB-012
  title: Can't look up or re-send an old receipt
  category: 1
  content: "Receipt history lives in the database, not on the printer and not in
    the current batch. If reprints and lookups fail while printing itself is fine,
    check POS Manager \u25B8 Connections for the database host.\nTypos in the host
    name are the usual cause and they are easy to skim past \u2014 compare it character
    by character against the correct address. A test page proves nothing here: it
    needs no transaction data, so it will pass happily while the record store is
    unreachable."
  relatedErrorCodes: []
  guidanceForIssueIds:
  - P12
